{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Occlusion Refinement.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Occlusion Refinement.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"occlusion refinement occlusion refinement","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Occlusion Refinement.md","fileName":"Occlusion Refinement.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Occlusion Refinement","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 21:16\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Augmented Reality Visual Coherence]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Augmented Reality Visual Coherence","augmentedreality_pearson.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Occlusion Refinement.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Occlusion Refinement.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"occlusion refinement occlusion refinement","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Occlusion Refinement.md","fileName":"Occlusion Refinement.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Occlusion Refinement","heading":"Occlusion Refinement","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Occlusion refinement improves the boundary where a coarse real-scene model decides visibility. The projected model supplies an initial contour, and evidence from the current camera image adjusts that contour toward the observed physical edge.\n\nThis lets a practical model support convincing masking without reproducing every surface detail. Refinement must remain temporally stable, since a boundary that changes unpredictably from frame to frame creates visible flicker.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Augmented Reality Visual Coherence","augmentedreality_pearson.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Occlusion Refinement.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Occlusion Refinement.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"occlusion refinement oc